id=a52sxq_e2e_optout_list
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: edge-to-edge opt-out list (Instagram black status bar)
author=kusti420
description=Android 16+ enforces edge-to-edge for apps targeting SDK 36 and ignores their windowOptOutEdgeToEdgeEnforcement; Instagram then draws a black strip under the status bar on its light UI (same on Pixels). Stock One UI hides this with a per-app "force opt-out of edge-to-edge" list (CoreRune FW_FORCE_OPT_OUT_EDGE_TO_EDGE, ActivityTaskManagerServiceExt.mForceOptOutEdgeToEdge) that SCPM downloads into /data/system/packageconfiguration - which never arrives on this port (verified 2026-11-01: the directory does not exist). This ships the list in /system/etc/k4/force_opt_out_e2e.txt and feeds it to the window manager at every boot through the framework's own shell command (`cmd window force-opt-out-e2e-add <pkg>`, WindowManagerShellCommand), in the shell domain like k4-wifiwatch. Tester report: "In Instagram the status bar turns black". Verify: Instagram (light theme) shows a white status bar; `cmd window force-opt-out-e2e-remove com.instagram.android` + relaunch brings the black strip back.
